  "body": "From #96 (PR #105). Verify now acquits a vertical dive into stock that an EARLIER op of the setup removed (rest::PriorPlan / verify::acquit_by_prior). But only Pocket3D's stamp includes the program ahead of it. If an earlier op (e.g. the Face) is later regenerated shallower, a later contour that was acquitted keeps reading Ok on a now-wrong verdict and posts - its dive goes into stock the face no longer removes. Not a regression (before #96 every vertical rapid was exempt).\n\nDone means: either the post gate re-checks the acquittal live against the current earlier ops, or every op's stamp includes a digest of the ops ahead of it (marks every non-first op of every saved project Stale once - say so in the release notes); pinned by face-then-contour where the face is regenerated shallower and the post refuses.",
